[90 16 "// the base type (Type())"] [91 16 "// its class"] [96 17 "// its own memory, else nil (a base's, an address's)"] [97 17 "// from_buffer's: the Python buffer's bytes mapped into the world, unmapped once collected"] [98 17 "// b_base"] [100 17 "// b_objects"] [102 2 "// a function pointer's state (PyCFuncPtrObject)"] [104 2 "// exports counts the memoryviews of the object not released (queue 260, py's BufferExports): CPython's CDataObject"] [105 2 "// has no ob_exports and ctypes.resize refuses nothing, so nothing here calls Refuse; the count is memoryview's"] [106 2 "// managed buffer's"] [112 1 "// The buffer protocol (queue 260): PyCData_NewGetBuffer. The view's bytes are the object's memory in the C world, read"] [113 1 "// and written in place (b_ptr, b_size); its format is the StgInfo's (\"B\" when it has none: a union, an incomplete"] [114 1 "// structure), its shape the StgInfo's (ndim its length), its itemsize the size of the innermost item type of an array"] [115 1 "// (PyCData_item_type), else of the type itself; never read-only."] [119 1 "// BytesLike is the object's memory (the C world's, in place)."] [127 1 "// WritableBytes is the same memory for writing (view->readonly = 0)."] [135 1 "// BufferShape is the view's format, itemsize and shape."] [160 1 "// rawMemory is the exporter of memoryview_at's view (PyMemoryView_FromMemory): size bytes of the world at ptr, read-only"] [161 1 "// unless writable."] [188 1 "// withFn gives a function pointer instance its PyCFuncPtrObject state (one made from memory: a result, a field)."] [196 1 "// obj is c as a Python object (its class's instance)."] [204 1 "// cdataOf is the CData of o (a ctypes instance), or nil."] [234 23 "// ctypes.ArgumentError"] [243 1 "// _ctypes_simple_instance: true for a subclass of c_int and the like (its base is not _SimpleCData), false for"] [244 1 "// c_int itself (callproc.c: such a class is kept as an instance, not converted by its getfunc)."] [249 1 "// tpName is a type's tp_name as CPython prints it in these messages (its __name__ for a heap type)."] [252 1 "// newCData is generic_pycdata_new / PyCData_MallocBuffer: a zeroed instance of t of its own memory."] [265 1 "// baseKind is the built-in base of a ctypes class."] [276 1 "// fromBaseObj is PyCData_FromBaseObj: an instance of t on base's memory at adr (base nil: a copy of adr's bytes)."] [294 1 "// atAddress is PyCData_AtAddress: an instance of t over the memory at buf."] [300 59 "// PyCData_AtAddress's audit (queue 598)"] [308 1 "// container is PyCData_GetContainer."] [334 1 "// keepRef is KeepRef."] [348 1 "// cdataGet is PyCData_get."] [361 1 "// cdataSetInner is _PyCData_set."] [403 1 "// cdataSet is PyCData_set."] [412 1 "// extendError is _ctypes_extend_error: the exception err re-raised as cls with prefix and \"ExcType: msg\"."] [425 1 "// ---- the metatypes ----"] [427 1 "// initTarget is the class a metatype's __init__ initializes: the metatypes' tp_new is type.__new__ alone and their"] [428 1 "// tp_init makes the StgInfo, as CPython's (metacls.__new__ without __init__ gives an abstract class); the init runs the"] [429 1 "// creation functions below on the class already made, which newClass hands them."] [432 1 "// newClass is type.__new__ for a metatype's class (the class being initialized when a metatype's __init__ runs)."] [451 1 "// simpleTypeNew is PyCSimpleType_new and PyCSimpleType_init."] [474 3 "// 3.15 (queue 252; _ctypes.c's PyCSimpleType_init): _ctypes_get_fielddesc takes the complex types' \"Zf\", \"Zd\","] [475 3 "// \"Zg\", which pyi's ffi does not have (Py_FFI_COMPLEX_AVAILABLE false): one AttributeError, ctypes' import catches it"] [495 2 "// the swapped variant for the byte orders (__ctype_be__, __ctype_le__), as PyCSimpleType_init's create_other_endian_type"] [496 2 "// PyCSimpleType_init: when the class's metatype is PyCSimpleType itself (not a subclass of it) and the code has"] [497 2 "// swapped accessors (queue 261: PyCSimpleType.__init__(cls, '', (), ns) on a class of no base gets them too)"] [519 1 "// makeSwapped is create_other_endian_type: a class of the same name with the byte-swapped accessors."] [528 2 "// CPython passes the class's own namespace (its __qualname__ kept) and the name with st->swapped_suffix (queue 260)"] [541 25 "// the swapped type is a class of its own: its StgInfo made afresh in CPython"] [551 1 "// fmtOf is the buffer format of a simple type's code (_ctypes_alloc_format_string_for_type)."] [553 2 "// queue 260: the standard-size code is ctypes' own but for i, I, l, L and ? (LP64, a 1-byte _Bool): c_char_p's"] [554 2 "// \"<z\", c_wchar's \"<u\", c_void_p's \"<P\" as CPython's"] [564 1 "// structTypeNew is PyCStructType_new/init (and UnionType's): the class, its StgInfo copied from its base's, its"] [565 1 "// _fields_ laid out when given."] [579 24 "// PyCStgInfo_clone: the cache cannot be shared (queue 261)"] [584 2 "// a class with _abstract_ in its namespace has no StgInfo (kept for compatibility: instantiating it is"] [585 2 "// \"abstract class\")"] [591 3 "// StructUnionType_init: PyObject_SetAttr, so a metaclass's __setattr__ sees them (queue 260: _endian.py's"] [592 3 "// _swapped_meta gives BigEndianStructure's fields their swapped types; pyi laid out the class's own)"] [601 1 "// updateStginfo is PyCStructUnionType_update_stginfo: the layout by ctypes._layout.get_layout, then the fields made"] [602 1 "// descriptors of the class (MakeAnonFields included)."] [706 2 "// the aggregate's ffi type (a union: its largest member's elements, stgdict.c's rule, as one struct)"] [713 2 "// a field of the class's own type marked it final during the layout (stgdict.c's check)"] [729 1 "// makeAnonFields is MakeAnonFields: the fields of each _anonymous_ field's type made the class's, at their offsets."] [757 1 "// makeFields is MakeFields: descr's type's fields as fields of t at offset."] [780 1 "// structTypeSetAttr is PyCStructType_setattro: _fields_ assigned lays the class out."] [799 1 "// arrayTypeNew is PyCArrayType_init."] [816 2 "// _PyLong_IsNegative before PyLong_AsSsize_t, as PyCArrayType_init: a huge negative length is a ValueError"] [854 2 "// char and wchar_t arrays: value and raw"] [868 1 "// pointerTypeNew is PyCPointerType_new/init."] [886 1 "// pointerSetProto is PyCPointerType_SetProto: the item type, and the item type's __pointer_type__."] [893 2 "// PyCPointerType_SetProto: \"&\" and the item's format (\"B\" for an incomplete type), its shape before it (queue 260)"] [914 1 "// funcPtrTypeNew is PyCFuncPtrType_new/init: _argtypes_, _restype_, _flags_."] [971 1 "// converters is converters_from_argtypes: each argtype's from_param."] [987 1 "// ---- CDataType's methods (on the metatypes) ----"] [1043 3 "// CPython shares the buffer's memory: a ctypes object's is the world's already; a Python buffer's bytes (Go"] [1044 3 "// memory) are mapped into the world (queue 261)"] [1079 3 "// CDataType_from_buffer_impl: a memoryview of the object (kept in _objects, so the exporter refuses a resize"] [1080 3 "// while the ctypes object lives), writable and C-contiguous; its bytes are mapped into the C world in place"] [1081 3 "// (queue 261: mapGo), so the ctypes object and the buffer share their memory as CPython's do"] [1136 64 "// CDataType_in_dll's audit (queue 598)"] [1177 1 "// arrayFromCtype is PyCArrayType_from_ctype: the class \"NAME_Array_N\", cached."] [1196 1 "// ---- CField ----"] [1267 20 "// a type used as a field's can no longer change its _fields_"] [1316 1 "// ---- instances ----"] [1318 1 "// simpleNew and genericNew are the types' tp_new."] [1361 1 "// structInit is Struct_init: positional arguments to the fields in order (the bases' first), keywords by name."] [1396 1 "// fieldNamesMRO: the names of the _fields_ of t and its bases, the bases' first (_init_pos_args)."] [1446 1 "// ---- arrays ----"] [1503 1 "// Slice_ is a slice's resolved indices."] [1580 1 "// ---- pointers ----"] [1643 1 "// ---- module functions -